  "id": "DrugBank_DB00719 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Azatadine is suggested to be associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis through a chain of indications that link it to familial dermatographia, a condition that is also linked to other compounds such as phenyltoloxamine, tripelennamine, and antazoline. These compounds are all indicated to cause vasomotor rhinitis, suggesting a potential mechanism where these substances may influence the vascular response in the nasal passages. The shared indication of vasomotor rhinitis across these compounds implies a possible overlapping pathway or mechanism that could be responsible for the observed association. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the hypothesis that Azatadine may share a similar mechanism of action or pathway with these other drugs in relation to vasomotor rhinitis. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a broader pharmacological relationship, though further research would be needed to confirm the exact mechanism and clinical relevance.",
